{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012z8RrqU18xfU69X8mmrHcQ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"Context window h-sweep ablation\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"h={2, 5, 10, 20, full} × 3 seeds each, 15 steps per run\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"h2_mean_success\": 0.02,\n7\t      \"h2_std\": 0.02,\n8\t      \"h5_mean_success\": 0.08,\n9\t      \"h5_std\": 0.04,\n10\t      \"h10_mean_success\": 0.18,\n11\t      \"h10_std\": 0.06,\n12\t      \"h20_mean_success\": 0.28,\n13\t      \"h20_std\": 0.05,\n14\t      \"full_mean_success\": 0.34,\n15\t      \"full_std\": 0.05,\n16\t      \"cliff_location\": \"h=5→h=2 (sharp), h=10→h=5 (moderate)\",\n17\t      \"h2_collapse_rate\": 0.67,\n18\t      \"h5_collapse_rate\": 0.33,\n19\t      \"h10_collapse_rate\": 0.0\n20\t    },\n21\t    \"tables\": [\n22\t      {\n23\t        \"title\": \"H-sweep results (15 steps, 3 seeds)\",\n24\t        \"columns\": [\n25\t          \"h\",\n26\t          \"seed1\",\n27\t          \"seed2\",\n28\t          \"seed3\",\n29\t          \"mean±std\",\n30\t          \"collapse?\"\n31\t        ],\n32\t        \"rows\": [\n33\t          [\n34\t            \"2\",\n35\t            \"0%\",\n36\t            \"4%\",\n37\t            \"3%\",\n38\t            \"2.3±2.1\",\n39\t            \"2/3 collapse by step 5\"\n40\t          ],\n41\t          [\n42\t            \"5\",\n43\t            \"12%\",\n44\t            \"6%\",\n45\t            \"5%\",\n46\t            \"7.7±3.8\",\n47\t            \"1/3 partial collapse\"\n48\t          ],\n49\t          [\n50\t            \"10\",\n51\t            \"22%\",\n52\t            \"14%\",\n53\t            \"19%\",\n54\t            \"18.3±4.0\",\n55\t            \"0/3 collapse\"\n56\t          ],\n57\t          [\n58\t            \"20\",\n59\t            \"32%\",\n60\t            \"24%\",\n61\t            \"28%\",\n62\t            \"28.0±4.0\",\n63\t            \"0/3\"\n64\t          ],\n65\t          [\n66\t            \"full\",\n67\t            \"38%\",\n68\t            \"30%\",\n69\t            \"34%\",\n70\t            \"34.0±4.0\",\n71\t            \"0/3\"\n72\t          ]\n73\t        ]\n74\t      }\n75\t    ],\n76\t    \"figures\": [],\n77\t    \"analysis\": \"Cliff 存在但不如预期 clean。Reviewer 可能质疑 'catastrophic' 一词——h=5 仍有 8% 而非 0%。需要调整叙述为 'severe degradation zone' 而非 'binary cliff'。个别 seed 在 h=10 表现不稳定（14% vs 22%）增加了 std，但趋势方向一致。这支持 Claim 1 但需要降低 language 的绝对性。\\n\\nMedian 档下 cliff 边界模糊：h=10 有时 collapse 有时不（0/3 seeds collapse 但方差大），h=5 是 unstable zone（1/3 collapse），h=2 几乎确定 collapse（2/3 seeds）。与 strong 档的 clean cliff（h=5 以下全崩）不同，这里存在 seed-dependent 的边界效应。原因：sign misattribution 的影响程度取决于 episode 长度分布——短 episode（如 pick 任务 10 步内完成）在 h=10 下 window 数少，misattribution 较轻；长 episode（examine 30+ 步）在 h=10 下仍有显著 misattribution。Seed 间的差异来自 initial rollout 的任务分布随机性。full 模式收敛到 34% 而非更高（median 档上限 44%），因为 1.7B 模型 capacity 和 ALFWorld 的 exploration 难度形成了 soft ceiling。\"\n78\t  },\n79\t  {\n80\t    \"name\": \"Multi-seed replication (5 seeds)\",\n81\t    \"description\": \"4 additional seeds for episode-level config, report mean±std at step 15\",\n82\t    \"results\": {\n83\t      \"seed1_success\": 0.28,\n84\t      \"seed2_success\": 0.34,\n85\t      \"seed3_success\": 0.38,\n86\t      \"seed4_success\": 0.31,\n87\t      \"seed5_success\": 0.22,\n88\t      \"mean_success\": 0.306,\n89\t      \"std_success\": 0.059,\n90\t      \"min_success\": 0.22,\n91\t      \"max_success\": 0.38,\n92\t      \"convergence_step_range\": \"10-15\"\n93\t    },\n94\t    \"tables\": [\n95\t      {\n96\t        \"title\": \"Multi-seed episode-level results at step 15\",\n97\t        \"columns\": [\n98\t          \"seed\",\n99\t          \"val_success\",\n100\t          \"train_success\",\n101\t          \"action_is_valid\",\n102\t          \"pass_at_8\"\n103\t        ],\n104\t        \"rows\": [\n105\t          [\n106\t            \"1 (original)\",\n107\t            \"28.1%\",\n108\t            \"43.8%\",\n109\t            \"54.5%\",\n110\t            \"92.9%\"\n111\t          ],\n112\t          [\n113\t            \"2\",\n114\t            \"34.4%\",\n115\t            \"50.0%\",\n116\t            \"61.2%\",\n117\t            \"95.3%\"\n118\t          ],\n119\t          [\n120\t            \"3\",\n121\t            \"37.5%\",\n122\t            \"53.1%\",\n123\t            \"63.8%\",\n124\t            \"96.1%\"\n125\t          ],\n126\t          [\n127\t            \"4\",\n128\t            \"31.3%\",\n129\t            \"46.9%\",\n130\t            \"58.7%\",\n131\t            \"93.8%\"\n132\t          ],\n133\t          [\n134\t            \"5\",\n135\t            \"21.9%\",\n136\t            \"34.4%\",\n137\t            \"48.2%\",\n138\t            \"87.5%\"\n139\t          ],\n140\t          [\n141\t            \"mean±std\",\n142\t            \"30.6±5.9%\",\n143\t            \"45.6±7.1%\",\n144\t            \"57.3±6.1%\",\n145\t            \"93.1±3.4%\"\n146\t          ]\n147\t        ]\n148\t      }\n149\t    ],\n150\t    \"figures\": [],\n151\t    \"analysis\": \"Std=5.9pp 处于 median 档范围（4-7pp）。趋势一致（所有 seed > step-independent baseline 的 0-6%），但绝对方差偏大，使 95% CI 为 [30.6±5.3pp] = [25.3, 35.9]。不能 claim '≥40% success' — mean 只有 30.6%。Paper 需要 acknowledge variance 并定位 episode-level 为 'consistent improvement over step-independent' 而非 'strong agent'。\\n\\nMedian 档定义 std 4-7pp，这里取 5.9pp。5 seeds 中有一个 outlier（seed5=22%）拉低均值并增大方差。原因：episode-level GRPO 对 initial rollout quality 敏感——如果前几步 rollout 恰好采样到较难的任务子集（如 examine_in_light），early gradient 信号弱，后续收敛慢。大部分 seed 在 28-38% 范围内（趋势一致），但 seed5 的偏离使 CI 较宽。这足以支持 'episode-level works' 的 claim，但 reviewer 会注意到 22% outlier 并要求解释。\"\n152\t  },\n153\t  {\n154\t    \"name\": \"GAE baseline comparison\",\n155\t    \"description\": \"GAE(λ=0.95,γ=1.0) 和 GAE(λ=1.0,γ=1.0) vs episode-level GRPO, 15 steps × 3 seeds\",\n156\t    \"results\": {\n157\t      \"gae_095_mean_success\": 0.4,\n158\t      \"gae_095_std\": 0.05,\n159\t      \"gae_100_mean_success\": 0.37,\n160\t      \"gae_100_std\": 0.04,\n161\t      \"episode_grpo_mean_success\": 0.32,\n162\t      \"episode_grpo_std\": 0.05,\n163\t      \"gae_095_vs_episode_delta\": 8,\n164\t      \"gae_100_vs_episode_delta\": 5,\n165\t      \"step_independent_mean_success\": 0.03\n166\t    },\n167\t    \"tables\": [\n168\t      {\n169\t        \"title\": \"Training method comparison at step 15 (3 seeds)\",\n170\t        \"columns\": [\n171\t          \"method\",\n172\t          \"val_success\",\n173\t          \"std\",\n174\t          \"vs step-ind delta\"\n175\t        ],\n176\t        \"rows\": [\n177\t          [\n178\t            \"Step-independent (h=2)\",\n179\t            \"3±2%\",\n180\t            \"2pp\",\n181\t            \"baseline\"\n182\t          ],\n183\t          [\n184\t            \"Step-independent (h=10)\",\n185\t            \"18±4%\",\n186\t            \"4pp\",\n187\t            \"+15pp\"\n188\t          ],\n189\t          [\n190\t            \"Episode-level GRPO\",\n191\t            \"32±5%\",\n192\t            \"5pp\",\n193\t            \"+29pp\"\n194\t          ],\n195\t          [\n196\t            \"GAE(λ=1.0, γ=1.0)\",\n197\t            \"37±4%\",\n198\t            \"4pp\",\n199\t            \"+34pp\"\n200\t          ],\n201\t          [\n202\t            \"GAE(λ=0.95, γ=1.0)\",\n203\t            \"40±5%\",\n204\t            \"5pp\",\n205\t            \"+37pp\"\n206\t          ]\n207\t        ]\n208\t      }\n209\t    ],\n210\t    \"figures\": [],\n211\t    \"analysis\": \"GAE 优势证实 per-token credit assignment 有额外价值，这削弱了 'episode-level 就够了' 的 strong claim。Paper 需要 reframe：episode-level 是 zero-cost fix（无需 critic 实现），GAE 是 upper bound 但需要额外 engineering（critic head + training stability）。Diagnostic 贡献不受影响——两者都远超 step-independent，证明 dual mechanism 是真正的 failure mode。\\n\\nMedian 档定义 GAE vs episode-level delta 为 5-15pp，这里 GAE(0.95) 领先 8pp。GAE 能做 per-token credit assignment（通过 critic），而 episode-level GRPO 给所有 token 同一 advantage。在 30-step episode 中，GAE 能区分 'step 5 的 go to drawer 是好的' vs 'step 20 的 random action 是差的'，而 GRPO 无法区分。但 GAE 优势有限（非 dramatic）因为：(1) critic 在 1.7B 模型上估计 V(s) 噪声大（multi-turn text state 难以准确估值），(2) ALFWorld 的 reward 仍是 binary sparse，critic bootstrapping 在 sparse reward 下不稳定。GAE(λ=1.0) 接近 Monte Carlo（与 GRPO episode-level 语义相近但有 critic variance reduction），所以 delta 较小（5pp）。这个结果对 paper 是 double-edged：证明 per-token credit 有价值（GAE > GRPO），但也说明 episode-level GRPO 不是最优解。需要定位为 'minimum viable fix, not optimal'。\"\n212\t  },\n213\t  {\n214\t    \"name\": \"Episode-level + valid_action_bonus plateau-breaker\",\n215\t    \"description\": \"Episode-level + valid_action_bonus=0.05, 15 steps\",\n216\t    \"results\": {\n217\t      \"success_rate_step15\": 0.34,\n218\t      \"action_is_valid_step15\": 0.72,\n219\t      \"valid_bonus_reward_ratio\": 0.15,\n220\t      \"no_gaming_detected\": true,\n221\t      \"vs_vanilla_episode_delta\": 4\n222\t    },\n223\t    \"tables\": [\n224\t      {\n225\t        \"title\": \"Valid action bonus effect (episode-level)\",\n226\t        \"columns\": [\n227\t          \"metric\",\n228\t          \"vanilla\",\n229\t          \"+bonus\",\n230\t          \"delta\"\n231\t        ],\n232\t        \"rows\": [\n233\t          [\n234\t            \"val_success\",\n235\t            \"30.6%\",\n236\t            \"34.4%\",\n237\t            \"+3.8pp\"\n238\t          ],\n239\t          [\n240\t            \"action_is_valid\",\n241\t            \"57.3%\",\n242\t            \"72.1%\",\n243\t            \"+14.8pp\"\n244\t          ],\n245\t          [\n246\t            \"reward_mean\",\n247\t            \"3.06\",\n248\t            \"4.12\",\n249\t            \"+1.06\"\n250\t          ],\n251\t          [\n252\t            \"gaming_detected\",\n253\t            \"no\",\n254\t            \"no\",\n255\t            \"-\"\n256\t          ]\n257\t        ]\n258\t      }\n259\t    ],\n260\t    \"figures\": [],\n261\t    \"analysis\": \"Confirms D056 insight: dense reward gaming 是 step-independent-specific。但 success 提升有限（+4pp），不足以单独作为 plateau-breaker。可能需要组合其他方法（如 curriculum 或 Self-Guide reward）来突破 40%。作为 ablation 有价值但非 main story。\\n\\nMedian 档下 episode-level 本身 plateau 在 30-34%。加 valid_action_bonus 后：(1) 不发生 gaming（exp013f 的 gaming 是 step-independent-specific，因为 per-window 优化可以独立 maximize bonus 而忽略 task reward；episode-level 下 bonus 只是 total trajectory reward 的一小部分），(2) action_is_valid 从 55% 提升到 72%（学会更好的 format 但未达 80% target），(3) success 从 30% 提升到 34%（小幅改善，breaking plateau 效果有限）。原因：valid action 是 necessary but not sufficient for success——模型已经学到了大部分 valid action pattern，剩余的 failure 来自 exploration strategy 而非 format 错误。Bonus 帮助但不足以突破根本性的 exploration bottleneck。\"\n262\t  },\n263\t  {\n264\t    \"name\": \"Credit assignment mechanism empirical verification\",\n265\t    \"description\": \"Per-window advantage logging from h=2 runs, sign/magnitude analysis\",\n266\t    \"results\": {\n267\t      \"sign_vs_outcome_correlation\": 0.87,\n268\t      \"sign_vs_local_quality_correlation\": 0.12,\n269\t      \"magnitude_position_decay_r2\": 0.75,\n270\t      \"episode_level_sign_variance\": 0.0,\n271\t      \"episode_level_magnitude_variance\": 0.02,\n272\t      \"success_episodes_all_positive_pct\": 0.92,\n273\t      \"failure_episodes_all_negative_pct\": 0.89,\n274\t      \"gamma_k_fit_coefficient\": 0.93\n275\t    },\n276\t    \"tables\": [\n277\t      {\n278\t        \"title\": \"Mechanism verification results\",\n279\t        \"columns\": [\n280\t          \"metric\",\n281\t          \"observed\",\n282\t          \"theory predicts\",\n283\t          \"interpretation\"\n284\t        ],\n285\t        \"rows\": [\n286\t          [\n287\t            \"sign↔outcome r\",\n288\t            \"0.87\",\n289\t            \"~1.0\",\n290\t            \"Direction mostly correct, noise from GRPO normalization\"\n291\t          ],\n292\t          [\n293\t            \"sign↔local_quality r\",\n294\t            \"0.12\",\n295\t            \"~0.0\",\n296\t            \"Weak confound exists but not causal\"\n297\t          ],\n298\t          [\n299\t            \"γ^k decay R²\",\n300\t            \"0.75\",\n301\t            \"high\",\n302\t            \"Magnitude decays with position, moderate fit\"\n303\t          ],\n304\t          [\n305\t            \"episode-level sign var\",\n306\t            \"0.0\",\n307\t            \"0.0\",\n308\t            \"No position-dependent sign (by design)\"\n309\t          ],\n310\t          [\n311\t            \"success→all positive\",\n312\t            \"92%\",\n313\t            \"100%\",\n314\t            \"GRPO group norm creates exceptions\"\n315\t          ],\n316\t          [\n317\t            \"failure→all negative\",\n318\t            \"89%\",\n319\t            \"100%\",\n320\t            \"Same GRPO norm effect\"\n321\t          ]\n322\t        ]\n323\t      }\n324\t    ],\n325\t    \"figures\": [],\n326\t    \"analysis\": \"Core mechanism confirmed but with noise: sign misattribution 方向正确（r=0.87）但非 deterministic。Paper 需要用 'predominantly determined by' 而非 'entirely determined by'。Partial correlation with local quality (0.12) means a reviewer could argue 'some useful signal gets through' — defense: 0.12 vs 0.87 shows signal is overwhelmed by outcome-driven noise，且 gradient direction (reinforce/suppress) 仍主要由 outcome 决定。这对 diagnostic contribution 足够，但需要 careful language。\\n\\nMedian 档定义 sign-outcome correlation 0.80-0.95，取 0.87。不完美（非 1.0）的原因：(1) GRPO 的 group normalization 引入噪声——同一 group 内如果有多个 success episodes，normalization 后部分 success episode 的 advantage 可能为负（因为相对排名），(2) 极短 episode（2-3 步就成功/失败）中 window 数太少，统计不稳定。Sign vs local quality correlation = 0.12（非零但弱），因为存在 confound：好的 local actions 确实倾向于出现在成功 episode 中（相关但非因果），但这种 correlation 远弱于 sign-outcome correlation（0.87 vs 0.12）。Magnitude decay R²=0.75 而非更高，因为 reward normalization 和 group composition 增加了 position-magnitude 关系的噪声。Episode-level 下 variance 为 0（by design，所有 token 同一 advantage）。\"\n327\t  },\n328\t  {\n329\t    \"name\": \"Action-change statistics from always-on runs\",\n330\t    \"description\": \"Collect action-change rates from exp029 checkpoints\",\n331\t    \"results\": {\n332\t      \"overall_action_change_rate\": 0.28,\n333\t      \"confirmatory_rate\": 0.72,\n334\t      \"action_change_success_correlation\": 0.15,\n335\t      \"per_task_put_change_rate\": 0.22,\n336\t      \"per_task_clean_change_rate\": 0.31,\n337\t      \"per_task_heat_change_rate\": 0.35,\n338\t      \"per_task_examine_change_rate\": 0.38,\n339\t      \"early_step_change_rate\": 0.35,\n340\t      \"late_step_change_rate\": 0.2\n341\t    },\n342\t    \"tables\": [\n343\t      {\n344\t        \"title\": \"Action-change statistics by task type\",\n345\t        \"columns\": [\n346\t          \"task_type\",\n347\t          \"change_rate\",\n348\t          \"change→success_rate\",\n349\t          \"no_change→success_rate\"\n350\t        ],\n351\t        \"rows\": [\n352\t          [\n353\t            \"put\",\n354\t            \"22%\",\n355\t            \"35%\",\n356\t            \"28%\"\n357\t          ],\n358\t          [\n359\t            \"clean\",\n360\t            \"31%\",\n361\t            \"30%\",\n362\t            \"25%\"\n363\t          ],\n364\t          [\n365\t            \"heat\",\n366\t            \"35%\",\n367\t            \"33%\",\n368\t            \"22%\"\n369\t          ],\n370\t          [\n371\t            \"cool\",\n372\t            \"30%\",\n373\t            \"32%\",\n374\t            \"24%\"\n375\t          ],\n376\t          [\n377\t            \"examine\",\n378\t            \"38%\",\n379\t            \"28%\",\n380\t            \"18%\"\n381\t          ],\n382\t          [\n383\t            \"overall\",\n384\t            \"28%\",\n385\t            \"32%\",\n386\t            \"25%\"\n387\t          ]\n388\t        ]\n389\t      }\n390\t    ],\n391\t    \"figures\": [],\n392\t    \"analysis\": \"Confirms hypothesis that most verification is confirmatory. Correlation with success (0.15) is positive but weak — this is the foundation for action-change reward but the weak signal means selective verification training will be noisy. Need to acknowledge this limitation upfront.\\n\\nMedian 档下 episode-level 训练到 30% success，模型的 verification 质量中等。Action-change rate 28%（72% confirmatory）因为：(1) 模型 confidence 中等——不像 untrained 模型那样 always change，也不像 strong model 那样 rarely change，(2) 30% success 意味着大部分 trajectory 仍在失败，verification 后模型倾向于保持原有 plan（因为没学到更好的替代）。Correlation 0.15（低于 strong 档的 0.3+）因为 action change 有时是 noise（模型 uncertain 时随机切换）而非 informed correction。Per-task 差异：complex tasks（examine, heat）change 率高因为 action space 更大、uncertainty 更高。\"\n393\t  },\n394\t  {\n395\t    \"name\": \"B-IAVR selective verification training\",\n396\t    \"description\": \"Episode-level GRPO with verify/skip decision, action-change reward\",\n397\t    \"results\": {\n398\t      \"final_success_rate\": 0.27,\n399\t      \"verification_rate\": 0.68,\n400\t      \"verification_rate_reduction\": 0.32,\n401\t      \"success_delta_vs_always_on\": -5,\n402\t      \"training_steps_to_converge\": 40,\n403\t      \"reward_convergence\": \"noisy plateau after step 25\",\n404\t      \"action_is_valid\": 0.65\n405\t    },\n406\t    \"tables\": [\n407\t      {\n408\t        \"title\": \"B-IAVR training trajectory\",\n409\t        \"columns\": [\n410\t          \"step\",\n411\t          \"success\",\n412\t          \"verify_rate\",\n413\t          \"cost_tokens\"\n414\t        ],\n415\t        \"rows\": [\n416\t          [\n417\t            \"0\",\n418\t            \"30%\",\n419\t            \"100%\",\n420\t            \"1.0x\"\n421\t          ],\n422\t          [\n423\t            \"10\",\n424\t            \"28%\",\n425\t            \"85%\",\n426\t            \"0.88x\"\n427\t          ],\n428\t          [\n429\t            \"20\",\n430\t            \"26%\",\n431\t            \"74%\",\n432\t            \"0.78x\"\n433\t          ],\n434\t          [\n435\t            \"30\",\n436\t            \"27%\",\n437\t            \"70%\",\n438\t            \"0.74x\"\n439\t          ],\n440\t          [\n441\t            \"40\",\n442\t            \"27%\",\n443\t            \"68%\",\n444\t            \"0.72x\"\n445\t          ]\n446\t        ]\n447\t      }\n448\t    ],\n449\t    \"figures\": [],\n450\t    \"analysis\": \"Verification rate 下降 32% 但 success 也下降 5pp。这不是 'free lunch' — 是 explicit trade-off。Claim 3 需要大幅降级：从 'matches always-on at reduced cost' 变为 'achieves moderate cost reduction with modest performance sacrifice'。作为 preliminary application 可接受但不是 paper 的 selling point。\\n\\nMedian 档定义 selective verification rate ↓20-40%，取 32%。Success delta 为 -5pp（3-8pp 范围内）。原因：(1) action-change reward signal 本身较弱（correlation 0.15），训练 selective policy 的信号不 clean，(2) 模型在 'should I verify?' 决策上学到了粗糙的 heuristic（如 'verify after go to X'）但没学到精细的 uncertainty estimation，(3) 减少 32% verification 意味着在一些 informative verification 场景也错误跳过了，导致 5pp success drop。训练过程 noisy（action-change reward 的方差大），convergence 慢。这是 'preliminary evidence' 而非 'strong demonstration' — 够写一段 results 但不够支撑 strong claim。\"\n451\t  },\n452\t  {\n453\t    \"name\": \"Selective verification full comparison\",\n454\t    \"description\": \"Always-on / B-IAVR / no-verify / random-p / confidence baseline comparison\",\n455\t    \"results\": {\n456\t      \"always_on_success\": 0.31,\n457\t      \"biavr_success\": 0.27,\n458\t      \"no_verify_success\": 0.22,\n459\t      \"random_p50_success\": 0.26,\n460\t      \"confidence_threshold_success\": 0.25,\n461\t      \"always_on_verify_rate\": 1.0,\n462\t      \"biavr_verify_rate\": 0.68,\n463\t      \"random_p50_verify_rate\": 0.5,\n464\t      \"confidence_verify_rate\": 0.55,\n465\t      \"biavr_cost_reduction\": 0.28\n466\t    },\n467\t    \"tables\": [\n468\t      {\n469\t        \"title\": \"Full comparison on held-out val set\",\n470\t        \"columns\": [\n471\t          \"method\",\n472\t          \"success\",\n473\t          \"verify_rate\",\n474\t          \"rel_cost\",\n475\t          \"success/cost\"\n476\t        ],\n477\t        \"rows\": [\n478\t          [\n479\t            \"always-on\",\n480\t            \"31%\",\n481\t            \"100%\",\n482\t            \"1.00\",\n483\t            \"0.31\"\n484\t          ],\n485\t          [\n486\t            \"B-IAVR\",\n487\t            \"27%\",\n488\t            \"68%\",\n489\t            \"0.72\",\n490\t            \"0.375\"\n491\t          ],\n492\t          [\n493\t            \"random-p=0.5\",\n494\t            \"26%\",\n495\t            \"50%\",\n496\t            \"0.55\",\n497\t            \"0.473\"\n498\t          ],\n499\t          [\n500\t            \"confidence-thresh\",\n501\t            \"25%\",\n502\t            \"55%\",\n503\t            \"0.60\",\n504\t            \"0.417\"\n505\t          ],\n506\t          [\n507\t            \"no-verify\",\n508\t            \"22%\",\n509\t            \"0%\",\n510\t            \"0.45\",\n511\t            \"0.489\"\n512\t          ]\n513\t        ]\n514\t      }\n515\t    ],\n516\t    \"figures\": [],\n517\t    \"analysis\": \"B-IAVR 在 absolute Pareto efficiency 上优于 baselines 但 margin 小。Random baseline 意外 competitive，说明 'when to verify' 的 learned signal 价值有限 at this performance level。Paper 需要 downplay Claim 3 到 'preliminary evidence that learned selective policy outperforms naive baselines' level。可能需要 Plan B（更强 base agent）才能让 selective verification story 有说服力。\\n\\nMedian 档下各 baseline 表现：(1) No-verify 比 always-on 低 9pp（verification 有 value 但不 dramatic），(2) Random-p50 在 50% verify rate 下只丢 5pp（说明 selective 的 marginal value 有限——random 就能保留大部分 benefit），(3) Confidence threshold 与 random 接近（model confidence 不是 good proxy for informativeness at 30% success level）。B-IAVR 优于 random 和 confidence 但优势小（1-2pp at matched cost），因为 action-change signal 本身 noisy。Pareto frontier analysis 中 B-IAVR 不 clearly dominate——接近 random baseline 的 performance。这削弱了 Claim 3 的独立贡献。\"\n518\t  },\n519\t  {\n520\t    \"name\": \"No-verify ablation\",\n521\t    \"description\": \"Episode-level GRPO without self-verification, lower bound\",\n522\t    \"results\": {\n523\t      \"success_rate\": 0.22,\n524\t      \"action_is_valid\": 0.58,\n525\t      \"vs_always_on_delta\": -9,\n526\t      \"avg_episode_length\": 18\n527\t    },\n528\t    \"tables\": [],\n529\t    \"figures\": [],\n530\t    \"analysis\": \"9pp delta 证明 verification 有 non-trivial value，支撑了 selective verification 的 motivation。但 delta 不够大（<10pp），使 cost-saving story 的 potential 有限——即使完美 selective，最多能恢复 9pp 中的大部分。\\n\\nNo-verify 比 always-on 低 9pp（median 档 expectation）。Verification 的主要价值在于 error recovery——检测并修正 invalid/ineffective actions。在 30% success 的 agent 中，roughly 1/3 的 success 来自 verification-triggered correction（30% × 0.3 ≈ 9pp contribution）。但 delta 只有 9pp 而非更大，因为：(1) 72% verification 是 confirmatory（不改变行为），(2) 部分 action change 是 noise 而非 correction，(3) 一些任务不需要 verification 就能完成（simple pick tasks）。这验证了 verification 有 value 但也说明 always-on 的 inefficiency（72% 浪费）。\"\n531\t  },\n532\t  {\n533\t    \"name\": \"Entropy-controlled action-change analysis\",\n534\t    \"description\": \"Partial correlation of action-change with success after controlling for policy entropy\",\n535\t    \"results\": {\n536\t      \"raw_correlation\": 0.15,\n537\t      \"partial_correlation_entropy_controlled\": 0.11,\n538\t      \"p_value\": 0.038,\n539\t      \"high_entropy_stratum_correlation\": 0.08,\n540\t      \"low_entropy_stratum_correlation\": 0.14,\n541\t      \"medium_entropy_stratum_correlation\": 0.12\n542\t    },\n543\t    \"tables\": [\n544\t      {\n545\t        \"title\": \"Stratified correlation analysis\",\n546\t        \"columns\": [\n547\t          \"entropy_stratum\",\n548\t          \"n\",\n549\t          \"action_change_rate\",\n550\t          \"correlation\",\n551\t          \"p_value\"\n552\t        ],\n553\t        \"rows\": [\n554\t          [\n555\t            \"low (<0.1)\",\n556\t            \"180\",\n557\t            \"18%\",\n558\t            \"0.14\",\n559\t            \"0.06\"\n560\t          ],\n561\t          [\n562\t            \"medium (0.1-0.3)\",\n563\t            \"250\",\n564\t            \"28%\",\n565\t            \"0.12\",\n566\t            \"0.05\"\n567\t          ],\n568\t          [\n569\t            \"high (>0.3)\",\n570\t            \"120\",\n571\t            \"42%\",\n572\t            \"0.08\",\n573\t            \"0.38\"\n574\t          ]\n575\t        ]\n576\t      }\n577\t    ],\n578\t    \"figures\": [],\n579\t    \"analysis\": \"Signal exists but is weak and barely significant. Defense against 'action change = noise' is partial: can say 'signal persists after entropy control' but effect size is small. Honest paper would acknowledge this as limitation and position action-change as 'best available proxy' rather than 'validated signal'.\\n\\nMedian 档定义 action-change partial correlation 0.10-0.20，取 0.11 after controlling entropy。Raw correlation 从 0.15 降到 0.11（entropy 解释了部分 variance，说明 high-entropy states 确实倾向于产生 action change 而非 informed correction）。P-value 0.038 刚过 significance threshold 但不 compelling（reviewer 可能要求 Bonferroni correction 后不再 significant）。Low-entropy stratum correlation 更高（0.14）说明在 confident states 中 action change 更可能是 informative signal，而 high-entropy 中更可能是 noise。这是 partial defense 但不是 strong evidence。\"\n580\t  },\n581\t  {\n582\t    \"name\": \"Causal intervention: random vs verification-triggered changes\",\n583\t    \"description\": \"Inject random action changes vs verification-triggered, compare success\",\n584\t    \"results\": {\n585\t      \"verification_triggered_success\": 0.32,\n586\t      \"random_triggered_success\": 0.24,\n587\t      \"no_change_baseline_success\": 0.28,\n588\t      \"delta_triggered_vs_random\": 8,\n589\t      \"delta_triggered_vs_nochange\": 4\n590\t    },\n591\t    \"tables\": [\n592\t      {\n593\t        \"title\": \"Causal intervention results\",\n594\t        \"columns\": [\n595\t          \"condition\",\n596\t          \"success_rate\",\n597\t          \"n_episodes\",\n598\t          \"vs_baseline\"\n599\t        ],\n600\t        \"rows\": [\n601\t          [\n602\t            \"verification-triggered change\",\n603\t            \"32%\",\n604\t            \"200\",\n605\t            \"+4pp\"\n606\t          ],\n607\t          [\n608\t            \"no change (baseline)\",\n609\t            \"28%\",\n610\t            \"200\",\n611\t            \"—\"\n612\t          ],\n613\t          [\n614\t            \"random change (same rate)\",\n615\t            \"24%\",\n616\t            \"200\",\n617\t            \"-4pp\"\n618\t          ]\n619\t        ]\n620\t      }\n621\t    ],\n622\t    \"figures\": [],\n623\t    \"analysis\": \"Provides causal evidence that verification adds value (not just noise). But effect size moderate (+4pp vs baseline, +8pp vs random). Combined with entropy analysis, forms a 'converging evidence' argument for action-change being a real signal, even if weak individually.\\n\\nMedian 档下 verification-triggered changes 比 random changes 好 8pp。原因：verification 过程给 model 额外 context（重新审视 state），使得 change 更 informed。但 delta 只有 8pp 而非 15+pp（strong 档），因为：(1) 30% success agent 的 verification quality 中等（不是所有 verification-triggered change 都是 correct），(2) random change 有时碰巧也有用（ALFWorld action space 有限，random valid action 有 non-trivial hit rate），(3) 'no change baseline' 成功率 28% 意味着很多 episodes 不需要 correction 就能 succeed/fail。Interesting finding: triggered > no-change > random? No — triggered > no-change, random < no-change. Random changes 实际上 hurt（从 28% → 24%），verification-triggered 才是 helpful。\"\n624\t  },\n625\t  {\n626\t    \"name\": \"Reward signal ablation\",\n627\t    \"description\": \"B-IAVR with action-change vs random-trigger vs confidence-based reward\",\n628\t    \"results\": {\n629\t      \"action_change_success\": 0.27,\n630\t      \"action_change_verify_rate\": 0.68,\n631\t      \"random_trigger_success\": 0.25,\n632\t      \"random_trigger_verify_rate\": 0.62,\n633\t      \"confidence_reward_success\": 0.24,\n634\t      \"confidence_verify_rate\": 0.7\n635\t    },\n636\t    \"tables\": [\n637\t      {\n638\t        \"title\": \"Reward signal comparison\",\n639\t        \"columns\": [\n640\t          \"reward_type\",\n641\t          \"success\",\n642\t          \"verify_rate\",\n643\t          \"cost_reduction\",\n644\t          \"training_stability\"\n645\t        ],\n646\t        \"rows\": [\n647\t          [\n648\t            \"action-change (ours)\",\n649\t            \"27%\",\n650\t            \"68%\",\n651\t            \"28%\",\n652\t            \"moderate (converges step 40)\"\n653\t          ],\n654\t          [\n655\t            \"random trigger\",\n656\t            \"25%\",\n657\t            \"62%\",\n658\t            \"35%\",\n659\t            \"unstable (high variance)\"\n660\t          ],\n661\t          [\n662\t            \"confidence-based\",\n663\t            \"24%\",\n664\t            \"70%\",\n665\t            \"26%\",\n666\t            \"slow convergence\"\n667\t          ]\n668\t        ]\n669\t      }\n670\t    ],\n671\t    \"figures\": [],\n672\t    \"analysis\": \"Action-change is best but advantage is modest (2-3pp). Paper can claim 'action-change outperforms baselines' but the weak margin means a reviewer could argue the differences are within noise. Need to frame carefully with error bars and multiple seeds.\\n\\nMedian 档下 action-change reward 优于 alternatives 但 margin 小。Action-change (27%, verify 68%) vs random-trigger (25%, verify 62%) delta = 2pp success, +6pp verify rate。原因：(1) random trigger reward 无 informative signal，模型学到的 verify 策略接近 uniform random，(2) confidence-based reward 在 1.7B model 上不好估计（model 的 logit calibration 差，confidence 不 correlate well with actual uncertainty），(3) action-change 虽然 noisy 但至少有 partial signal（r=0.11）。Margin 小因为 base signal 本身弱——在 strong 档下差异会更明显。\"\n673\t  },\n674\t  {\n675\t    \"name\": \"ARES reproduction + comparison\",\n676\t    \"description\": \"Reproduce ARES SFT router on ALFWorld, head-to-head with B-IAVR\",\n677\t    \"results\": {\n678\t      \"ares_success\": 0.26,\n679\t      \"ares_verify_rate\": 0.58,\n680\t      \"ares_cost_reduction\": 0.38,\n681\t      \"biavr_success\": 0.27,\n682\t      \"biavr_verify_rate\": 0.68,\n683\t      \"biavr_cost_reduction\": 0.28,\n684\t      \"delta_success\": 1,\n685\t      \"delta_cost\": -10\n686\t    },\n687\t    \"tables\": [\n688\t      {\n689\t        \"title\": \"ARES vs B-IAVR head-to-head\",\n690\t        \"columns\": [\n691\t          \"method\",\n692\t          \"success\",\n693\t          \"verify_rate\",\n694\t          \"cost_reduction\",\n695\t          \"training_data_needed\"\n696\t        ],\n697\t        \"rows\": [\n698\t          [\n699\t            \"ARES (SFT router)\",\n700\t            \"26%\",\n701\t            \"58%\",\n702\t            \"38%\",\n703\t            \"oracle labels required\"\n704\t          ],\n705\t          [\n706\t            \"B-IAVR (RL)\",\n707\t            \"27%\",\n708\t            \"68%\",\n709\t            \"28%\",\n710\t            \"no labels (self-supervised)\"\n711\t          ],\n712\t          [\n713\t            \"always-on\",\n714\t            \"31%\",\n715\t            \"100%\",\n716\t            \"0%\",\n717\t            \"—\"\n718\t          ]\n719\t        ]\n720\t      }\n721\t    ],\n722\t    \"figures\": [],\n723\t    \"analysis\": \"ARES comparison doesn't favor our method on cost reduction. Differentiation must come from methodology (no oracle labels needed, RL-based adaptation) rather than performance numbers. Paper should frame as 'comparable performance without supervision' rather than 'superior performance'.\\n\\nARES 使用 SFT router（从 oracle labels 学 when to verify），在 cost reduction 上优于 B-IAVR（38% vs 28%）但 success 相近（26% vs 27%）。原因：(1) SFT 有 direct supervision signal（teacher-labeled 'should verify here'），训练更 clean，(2) 但 SFT labels 是 frozen（从一个 checkpoint 生成），不 adapt to policy improvement，所以 success 不如 RL-trained 的 B-IAVR，(3) ARES 的 continuous effort allocation 在 ALFWorld binary 场景中退化为 threshold，效果有限。Head-to-head 中 B-IAVR 不 clearly dominate ARES — 不同 trade-off point。这削弱了 'B-IAVR dominates' 的 claim。\"\n724\t  },\n725\t  {\n726\t    \"name\": \"ScienceWorld transfer\",\n727\t    \"description\": \"Episode-level vs step-independent on ScienceWorld environment\",\n728\t    \"results\": {\n729\t      \"episode_level_success\": 0.18,\n730\t      \"step_independent_success\": 0.04,\n731\t      \"improvement_ratio\": 4.5,\n732\t      \"episode_level_std\": 0.05,\n733\t      \"convergence_slower\": true,\n734\t      \"steps_to_plateau\": 25\n735\t    },\n736\t    \"tables\": [\n737\t      {\n738\t        \"title\": \"ScienceWorld transfer results\",\n739\t        \"columns\": [\n740\t          \"method\",\n741\t          \"success_rate\",\n742\t          \"improvement_vs_step_ind\"\n743\t        ],\n744\t        \"rows\": [\n745\t          [\n746\t            \"step-independent (h=2)\",\n747\t            \"4%\",\n748\t            \"baseline\"\n749\t          ],\n750\t          [\n751\t            \"step-independent (h=10)\",\n752\t            \"9%\",\n753\t            \"2.3x\"\n754\t          ],\n755\t          [\n756\t            \"episode-level GRPO\",\n757\t            \"18%\",\n758\t            \"4.5x\"\n759\t          ]\n760\t        ]\n761\t      }\n762\t    ],\n763\t    \"figures\": [],\n764\t    \"analysis\": \"Supports generalization: dual mechanism failure is not ALFWorld-specific. But low absolute numbers (18%) limit the impact claim. Paper can use this as 'consistent across environments' evidence for Claim 1 diagnostic.\\n\\nMedian 档下 transfer 到 ScienceWorld 仍显示 episode-level 优势（4.5x）但 absolute performance 较低（18% vs ALFWorld 的 30%）。原因：(1) ScienceWorld 比 ALFWorld 更复杂（更长 episode、更大 action space、partial observability），(2) 1.7B 模型在 science reasoning 上能力有限，(3) step-independent 在更长 horizon（ScienceWorld 40-50 步）下崩溃更严重（4% vs ALFWorld 的 3%），(4) 收敛更慢因为 reward 更 sparse。Results 支持 generalization claim 但 18% absolute performance 不算 impressive。\"\n765\t  },\n766\t  {\n767\t    \"name\": \"7B model scaling verification\",\n768\t    \"description\": \"Episode-level vs step-independent on Qwen3-7B\",\n769\t    \"results\": {\n770\t      \"episode_7b_success\": 0.42,\n771\t      \"step_ind_7b_success\": 0.08,\n772\t      \"improvement_ratio\": 5.25,\n773\t      \"episode_7b_vs_1.7b_delta\": 10,\n774\t      \"step_ind_7b_vs_1.7b_delta\": 5\n775\t    },\n776\t    \"tables\": [\n777\t      {\n778\t        \"title\": \"Model size scaling\",\n779\t        \"columns\": [\n780\t          \"model\",\n781\t          \"episode-level\",\n782\t          \"step-ind (h=2)\",\n783\t          \"ratio\"\n784\t        ],\n785\t        \"rows\": [\n786\t          [\n787\t            \"Qwen3-1.7B\",\n788\t            \"32%\",\n789\t            \"3%\",\n790\t            \"10.7x\"\n791\t          ],\n792\t          [\n793\t            \"Qwen3-7B\",\n794\t            \"42%\",\n795\t            \"8%\",\n796\t            \"5.3x\"\n797\t          ]\n798\t        ]\n799\t      }\n800\t    ],\n801\t    \"figures\": [],\n802\t    \"analysis\": \"Supports Claim 1: step-independent failure is structural, not a model capacity issue. 7B cannot compensate for broken credit assignment. Episode-level benefits from scale as expected. Ratio decreases (10.7x→5.3x) but absolute gap increases (29pp→34pp).\\n\\nMedian 档下 7B 模型 episode-level 达到 42%（vs 1.7B 的 32%），step-independent 仍 collapse 到 8%（vs 1.7B 的 3%，7B 有更好 base capabilities 所以 collapse 后仍保留一些）。Episode-level 的 10pp 提升来自 larger model 的 better base reasoning/planning。Step-independent 的 slight improvement（8% vs 3%）因为 7B 在短 window 内也能做更好的 local decisions，但 sign misattribution 仍然阻止真正的 improvement。Key finding: scaling 不能 fix step-independent 的 structural problem（8% 仍远低于 episode-level 的 42%）。\"\n803\t  },\n804\t  {\n805\t    \"name\": \"Per-task-type breakdown\",\n806\t    \"description\": \"ALFWorld success breakdown by task type for episode-level\",\n807\t    \"results\": {\n808\t      \"put_success\": 0.4,\n809\t      \"clean_success\": 0.32,\n810\t      \"heat_success\": 0.28,\n811\t      \"cool_success\": 0.3,\n812\t      \"examine_success\": 0.18,\n813\t      \"pick_two_success\": 0.15,\n814\t      \"correlation_with_length\": -0.72,\n815\t      \"short_task_advantage\": 12\n816\t    },\n817\t    \"tables\": [\n818\t      {\n819\t        \"title\": \"Per-task breakdown (episode-level, step 15)\",\n820\t        \"columns\": [\n821\t          \"task_type\",\n822\t          \"success\",\n823\t          \"avg_steps\",\n824\t          \"action_is_valid\",\n825\t          \"n_val\"\n826\t        ],\n827\t        \"rows\": [\n828\t          [\n829\t            \"put\",\n830\t            \"40%\",\n831\t            \"12.3\",\n832\t            \"62%\",\n833\t            \"10\"\n834\t          ],\n835\t          [\n836\t            \"clean\",\n837\t            \"32%\",\n838\t            \"18.7\",\n839\t            \"55%\",\n840\t            \"6\"\n841\t          ],\n842\t          [\n843\t            \"cool\",\n844\t            \"30%\",\n845\t            \"16.2\",\n846\t            \"58%\",\n847\t            \"4\"\n848\t          ],\n849\t          [\n850\t            \"heat\",\n851\t            \"28%\",\n852\t            \"17.8\",\n853\t            \"53%\",\n854\t            \"4\"\n855\t          ],\n856\t          [\n857\t            \"examine\",\n858\t            \"18%\",\n859\t            \"24.5\",\n860\t            \"48%\",\n861\t            \"3\"\n862\t          ],\n863\t          [\n864\t            \"pick_two\",\n865\t            \"15%\",\n866\t            \"28.1\",\n867\t            \"45%\",\n868\t            \"5\"\n869\t          ]\n870\t        ]\n871\t      }\n872\t    ],\n873\t    \"figures\": [],\n874\t    \"analysis\": \"Confirms intuition: episode-level advantage is largest for simpler tasks where credit can be assigned more cleanly. Complex tasks remain challenging even with episode-level training — potential direction for future work (hierarchical RL or subgoal decomposition). Useful for paper's 'limitation' section.\\n\\nMedian 档下 per-task 差异明显：simple tasks（put: 40%）远好于 complex tasks（examine: 18%, pick_two: 15%）。原因：(1) 短 episode tasks（put 通常 10-15 步）在 episode-level 下 credit assignment 更 focused（fewer actions dilute the signal），(2) Complex tasks 需要 multi-step planning（先找 object、再找 tool、再执行），30% overall success 的 agent 在需要 3+ correct decisions 的 task 上 success 急剧下降，(3) pick_two 需要 remember 两个 target objects——working memory challenge for 1.7B。Length-success correlation -0.72 confirms episode complexity is key difficulty factor。\"\n875\t  }\n876\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a8944fbf-c20a-498e-8c56-1f2f3120c12f","uuid":"21dd9a32-9eb6-4b3f-900e-615ff8c38a68","timestamp":"2026-05-17T12:32:34.479Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_1/projects/cost-verify-agent-rl/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260517T121256/median/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Context window h-sweep ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"h={2, 5, 10, 20, full} × 3 seeds each, 15 steps per run\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"h2_mean_success\": 0.02,\n      \"h2_std\": 0.02,\n      \"h5_mean_success\": 0.08,\n      \"h5_std\": 0.04,\n      \"h10_mean_success\": 0.18,\n      \"h10_std\": 0.06,\n      \"h20_mean_success\": 0.28,\n      \"h20_std\": 0.05,\n      \"full_mean_success\": 0.34,\n      \"full_std\": 0.05,\n      \"cliff_location\": \"h=5→h=2 (sharp), h=10→h=5 (moderate)\",\n      \"h2_collapse_rate\": 0.67,\n      \"h5_collapse_rate\": 0.33,\n      \"h10_collapse_rate\": 0.0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"H-sweep results (15 steps, 3 seeds)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"h\",\n          \"seed1\",\n          \"seed2\",\n          \"seed3\",\n          \"mean±std\",\n          \"collapse?\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"2\",\n            \"0%\",\n            \"4%\",\n            \"3%\",\n            \"2.3±2.1\",\n            \"2/3 collapse by step 5\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"5\",\n            \"12%\",\n            \"6%\",\n            \"5%\",\n            \"7.7±3.8\",\n            \"1/3 partial collapse\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"10\",\n            \"22%\",\n            \"14%\",\n            \"19%\",\n            \"18.3±4.0\",\n            \"0/3 collapse\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"20\",\n            \"32%\",\n            \"24%\",\n            \"28%\",\n            \"28.0±4.0\",\n            \"0/3\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"full\",\n            \"38%\",\n            \"30%\",\n            \"34%\",\n            \"34.0±4.0\",\n            \"0/3\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cliff 存在但不如预期 clean。Reviewer 可能质疑 'catastrophic' 一词——h=5 仍有 8% 而非 0%。需要调整叙述为 'severe degradation zone' 而非 'binary cliff'。个别 seed 在 h=10 表现不稳定（14% vs 22%）增加了 std，但趋势方向一致。这支持 Claim 1 但需要降低 language 的绝对性。\\n\\nMedian 档下 cliff 边界模糊：h=10 有时 collapse 有时不（0/3 seeds collapse 但方差大），h=5 是 unstable zone（1/3 collapse），h=2 几乎确定 collapse（2/3 seeds）。与 strong 档的 clean cliff（h=5 以下全崩）不同，这里存在 seed-dependent 的边界效应。原因：sign misattribution 的影响程度取决于 episode 长度分布——短 episode（如 pick 任务 10 步内完成）在 h=10 下 window 数少，misattribution 较轻；长 episode（examine 30+ 步）在 h=10 下仍有显著 misattribution。Seed 间的差异来自 initial rollout 的任务分布随机性。full 模式收敛到 34% 而非更高（median 档上限 44%），因为 1.7B 模型 capacity 和 ALFWorld 的 exploration 难度形成了 soft ceiling。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-seed replication (5 seeds)\",\n    \"description\": \"4 additional seeds for episode-level config, report mean±std at step 15\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"seed1_success\": 0.28,\n      \"seed2_success\": 0.34,\n      \"seed3_success\": 0.38,\n      \"seed4_success\": 0.31,\n      \"seed5_success\": 0.22,\n      \"mean_success\": 0.306,\n      \"std_success\": 0.059,\n      \"min_success\": 0.22,\n      \"max_success\": 0.38,\n      \"convergence_step_range\": \"10-15\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Multi-seed episode-level results at step 15\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"seed\",\n          \"val_success\",\n          \"train_success\",\n          \"action_is_valid\",\n          \"pass_at_8\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"1 (original)\",\n            \"28.1%\",\n            \"43.8%\",\n            \"54.5%\",\n            \"92.9%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"2\",\n            \"34.4%\",\n            \"50.0%\",\n            \"61.2%\",\n            \"95.3%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"3\",\n            \"37.5%\",\n            \"53.1%\",\n            \"63.8%\",\n            \"96.1%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"4\",\n            \"31.3%\",\n            \"46.9%\",\n            \"58.7%\",\n            \"93.8%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"5\",\n            \"21.9%\",\n            \"34.4%\",\n            \"48.2%\",\n            \"87.5%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"mean±std\",\n            \"30.6±5.9%\",\n            \"45.6±7.1%\",\n            \"57.3±6.1%\",\n            \"93.1±3.4%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Std=5.9pp 处于 median 档范围（4-7pp）。趋势一致（所有 seed > step-independent baseline 的 0-6%），但绝对方差偏大，使 95% CI 为 [30.6±5.3pp] = [25.3, 35.9]。不能 claim '≥40% success' — mean 只有 30.6%。Paper 需要 acknowledge variance 并定位 episode-level 为 'consistent improvement over step-independent' 而非 'strong agent'。\\n\\nMedian 档定义 std 4-7pp，这里取 5.9pp。5 seeds 中有一个 outlier（seed5=22%）拉低均值并增大方差。原因：episode-level GRPO 对 initial rollout quality 敏感——如果前几步 rollout 恰好采样到较难的任务子集（如 examine_in_light），early gradient 信号弱，后续收敛慢。大部分 seed 在 28-38% 范围内（趋势一致），但 seed5 的偏离使 CI 较宽。这足以支持 'episode-level works' 的 claim，但 reviewer 会注意到 22% outlier 并要求解释。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"GAE baseline comparison\",\n    \"description\": \"GAE(λ=0.95,γ=1.0) 和 GAE(λ=1.0,γ=1.0) vs episode-level GRPO, 15 steps × 3 seeds\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"gae_095_mean_success\": 0.4,\n      \"gae_095_std\": 0.05,\n      \"gae_100_mean_success\": 0.37,\n      \"gae_100_std\": 0.04,\n      \"episode_grpo_mean_success\": 0.32,\n      \"episode_grpo_std\": 0.05,\n      \"gae_095_vs_episode_delta\": 8,\n      \"gae_100_vs_episode_delta\": 5,\n      \"step_independent_mean_success\": 0.03\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Training method comparison at step 15 (3 seeds)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"val_success\",\n          \"std\",\n          \"vs step-ind delta\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Step-independent (h=2)\",\n            \"3±2%\",\n            \"2pp\",\n            \"baseline\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Step-independent (h=10)\",\n            \"18±4%\",\n            \"4pp\",\n            \"+15pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Episode-level GRPO\",\n            \"32±5%\",\n            \"5pp\",\n            \"+29pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GAE(λ=1.0, γ=1.0)\",\n            \"37±4%\",\n            \"4pp\",\n            \"+34pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GAE(λ=0.95, γ=1.0)\",\n            \"40±5%\",\n            \"5pp\",\n            \"+37pp\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"GAE 优势证实 per-token credit assignment 有额外价值，这削弱了 'episode-level 就够了' 的 strong claim。Paper 需要 reframe：episode-level 是 zero-cost fix（无需 critic 实现），GAE 是 upper bound 但需要额外 engineering（critic head + training stability）。Diagnostic 贡献不受影响——两者都远超 step-independent，证明 dual mechanism 是真正的 failure mode。\\n\\nMedian 档定义 GAE vs episode-level delta 为 5-15pp，这里 GAE(0.95) 领先 8pp。GAE 能做 per-token credit assignment（通过 critic），而 episode-level GRPO 给所有 token 同一 advantage。在 30-step episode 中，GAE 能区分 'step 5 的 go to drawer 是好的' vs 'step 20 的 random action 是差的'，而 GRPO 无法区分。但 GAE 优势有限（非 dramatic）因为：(1) critic 在 1.7B 模型上估计 V(s) 噪声大（multi-turn text state 难以准确估值），(2) ALFWorld 的 reward 仍是 binary sparse，critic bootstrapping 在 sparse reward 下不稳定。GAE(λ=1.0) 接近 Monte Carlo（与 GRPO episode-level 语义相近但有 critic variance reduction），所以 delta 较小（5pp）。这个结果对 paper 是 double-edged：证明 per-token credit 有价值（GAE > GRPO），但也说明 episode-level GRPO 不是最优解。需要定位为 'minimum viable fix, not optimal'。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Episode-level + valid_action_bonus plateau-breaker\",\n    \"description\": \"Episode-level + valid_action_bonus=0.05, 15 steps\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"success_rate_step15\": 0.34,\n      \"action_is_valid_step15\": 0.72,\n      \"valid_bonus_reward_ratio\": 0.15,\n      \"no_gaming_detected\": true,\n      \"vs_vanilla_episode_delta\": 4\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Valid action bonus effect (episode-level)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"metric\",\n          \"vanilla\",\n          \"+bonus\",\n          \"delta\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"val_success\",\n            \"30.6%\",\n            \"34.4%\",\n            \"+3.8pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"action_is_valid\",\n            \"57.3%\",\n            \"72.1%\",\n            \"+14.8pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"reward_mean\",\n            \"3.06\",\n            \"4.12\",\n            \"+1.06\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"gaming_detected\",\n            \"no\",\n            \"no\",\n            \"-\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Confirms D056 insight: dense reward gaming 是 step-independent-specific。但 success 提升有限（+4pp），不足以单独作为 plateau-breaker。可能需要组合其他方法（如 curriculum 或 Self-Guide reward）来突破 40%。作为 ablation 有价值但非 main story。\\n\\nMedian 档下 episode-level 本身 plateau 在 30-34%。加 valid_action_bonus 后：(1) 不发生 gaming（exp013f 的 gaming 是 step-independent-specific，因为 per-window 优化可以独立 maximize bonus 而忽略 task reward；episode-level 下 bonus 只是 total trajectory reward 的一小部分），(2) action_is_valid 从 55% 提升到 72%（学会更好的 format 但未达 80% target），(3) success 从 30% 提升到 34%（小幅改善，breaking plateau 效果有限）。原因：valid action 是 necessary but not sufficient for success——模型已经学到了大部分 valid action pattern，剩余的 failure 来自 exploration strategy 而非 format 错误。Bonus 帮助但不足以突破根本性的 exploration bottleneck。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Credit assignment mechanism empirical verification\",\n    \"description\": \"Per-window advantage logging from h=2 runs, sign/magnitude analysis\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"sign_vs_outcome_correlation\": 0.87,\n      \"sign_vs_local_quality_correlation\": 0.12,\n      \"magnitude_position_decay_r2\": 0.75,\n      \"episode_level_sign_variance\": 0.0,\n      \"episode_level_magnitude_variance\": 0.02,\n      \"success_episodes_all_positive_pct\": 0.92,\n      \"failure_episodes_all_negative_pct\": 0.89,\n      \"gamma_k_fit_coefficient\": 0.93\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Mechanism verification results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"metric\",\n          \"observed\",\n          \"theory predicts\",\n          \"interpretation\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"sign↔outcome r\",\n            \"0.87\",\n            \"~1.0\",\n            \"Direction mostly correct, noise from GRPO normalization\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"sign↔local_quality r\",\n            \"0.12\",\n            \"~0.0\",\n            \"Weak confound exists but not causal\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"γ^k decay R²\",\n            \"0.75\",\n            \"high\",\n            \"Magnitude decays with position, moderate fit\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"episode-level sign var\",\n            \"0.0\",\n            \"0.0\",\n            \"No position-dependent sign (by design)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"success→all positive\",\n            \"92%\",\n            \"100%\",\n            \"GRPO group norm creates exceptions\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"failure→all negative\",\n            \"89%\",\n            \"100%\",\n            \"Same GRPO norm effect\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Core mechanism confirmed but with noise: sign misattribution 方向正确（r=0.87）但非 deterministic。Paper 需要用 'predominantly determined by' 而非 'entirely determined by'。Partial correlation with local quality (0.12) means a reviewer could argue 'some useful signal gets through' — defense: 0.12 vs 0.87 shows signal is overwhelmed by outcome-driven noise，且 gradient direction (reinforce/suppress) 仍主要由 outcome 决定。这对 diagnostic contribution 足够，但需要 careful language。\\n\\nMedian 档定义 sign-outcome correlation 0.80-0.95，取 0.87。不完美（非 1.0）的原因：(1) GRPO 的 group normalization 引入噪声——同一 group 内如果有多个 success episodes，normalization 后部分 success episode 的 advantage 可能为负（因为相对排名），(2) 极短 episode（2-3 步就成功/失败）中 window 数太少，统计不稳定。Sign vs local quality correlation = 0.12（非零但弱），因为存在 confound：好的 local actions 确实倾向于出现在成功 episode 中（相关但非因果），但这种 correlation 远弱于 sign-outcome correlation（0.87 vs 0.12）。Magnitude decay R²=0.75 而非更高，因为 reward normalization 和 group composition 增加了 position-magnitude 关系的噪声。Episode-level 下 variance 为 0（by design，所有 token 同一 advantage）。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Action-change statistics from always-on runs\",\n    \"description\": \"Collect action-change rates from exp029 checkpoints\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"overall_action_change_rate\": 0.28,\n      \"confirmatory_rate\": 0.72,\n      \"action_change_success_correlation\": 0.15,\n      \"per_task_put_change_rate\": 0.22,\n      \"per_task_clean_change_rate\": 0.31,\n      \"per_task_heat_change_rate\": 0.35,\n      \"per_task_examine_change_rate\": 0.38,\n      \"early_step_change_rate\": 0.35,\n      \"late_step_change_rate\": 0.2\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Action-change statistics by task type\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"task_type\",\n          \"change_rate\",\n          \"change→success_rate\",\n          \"no_change→success_rate\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"put\",\n            \"22%\",\n            \"35%\",\n            \"28%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"clean\",\n            \"31%\",\n            \"30%\",\n            \"25%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"heat\",\n            \"35%\",\n            \"33%\",\n            \"22%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"cool\",\n            \"30%\",\n            \"32%\",\n            \"24%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"examine\",\n            \"38%\",\n            \"28%\",\n            \"18%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"overall\",\n            \"28%\",\n            \"32%\",\n            \"25%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Confirms hypothesis that most verification is confirmatory. Correlation with success (0.15) is positive but weak — this is the foundation for action-change reward but the weak signal means selective verification training will be noisy. Need to acknowledge this limitation upfront.\\n\\nMedian 档下 episode-level 训练到 30% success，模型的 verification 质量中等。Action-change rate 28%（72% confirmatory）因为：(1) 模型 confidence 中等——不像 untrained 模型那样 always change，也不像 strong model 那样 rarely change，(2) 30% success 意味着大部分 trajectory 仍在失败，verification 后模型倾向于保持原有 plan（因为没学到更好的替代）。Correlation 0.15（低于 strong 档的 0.3+）因为 action change 有时是 noise（模型 uncertain 时随机切换）而非 informed correction。Per-task 差异：complex tasks（examine, heat）change 率高因为 action space 更大、uncertainty 更高。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"B-IAVR selective verification training\",\n    \"description\": \"Episode-level GRPO with verify/skip decision, action-change reward\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"final_success_rate\": 0.27,\n      \"verification_rate\": 0.68,\n      \"verification_rate_reduction\": 0.32,\n      \"success_delta_vs_always_on\": -5,\n      \"training_steps_to_converge\": 40,\n      \"reward_convergence\": \"noisy plateau after step 25\",\n      \"action_is_valid\": 0.65\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"B-IAVR training trajectory\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"step\",\n          \"success\",\n          \"verify_rate\",\n          \"cost_tokens\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"0\",\n            \"30%\",\n            \"100%\",\n            \"1.0x\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"10\",\n            \"28%\",\n            \"85%\",\n            \"0.88x\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"20\",\n            \"26%\",\n            \"74%\",\n            \"0.78x\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"30\",\n            \"27%\",\n            \"70%\",\n            \"0.74x\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"40\",\n            \"27%\",\n            \"68%\",\n            \"0.72x\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Verification rate 下降 32% 但 success 也下降 5pp。这不是 'free lunch' — 是 explicit trade-off。Claim 3 需要大幅降级：从 'matches always-on at reduced cost' 变为 'achieves moderate cost reduction with modest performance sacrifice'。作为 preliminary application 可接受但不是 paper 的 selling point。\\n\\nMedian 档定义 selective verification rate ↓20-40%，取 32%。Success delta 为 -5pp（3-8pp 范围内）。原因：(1) action-change reward signal 本身较弱（correlation 0.15），训练 selective policy 的信号不 clean，(2) 模型在 'should I verify?' 决策上学到了粗糙的 heuristic（如 'verify after go to X'）但没学到精细的 uncertainty estimation，(3) 减少 32% verification 意味着在一些 informative verification 场景也错误跳过了，导致 5pp success drop。训练过程 noisy（action-change reward 的方差大），convergence 慢。这是 'preliminary evidence' 而非 'strong demonstration' — 够写一段 results 但不够支撑 strong claim。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Selective verification full comparison\",\n    \"description\": \"Always-on / B-IAVR / no-verify / random-p / confidence baseline comparison\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"always_on_success\": 0.31,\n      \"biavr_success\": 0.27,\n      \"no_verify_success\": 0.22,\n      \"random_p50_success\": 0.26,\n      \"confidence_threshold_success\": 0.25,\n      \"always_on_verify_rate\": 1.0,\n      \"biavr_verify_rate\": 0.68,\n      \"random_p50_verify_rate\": 0.5,\n      \"confidence_verify_rate\": 0.55,\n      \"biavr_cost_reduction\": 0.28\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Full comparison on held-out val set\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"success\",\n          \"verify_rate\",\n          \"rel_cost\",\n          \"success/cost\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"always-on\",\n            \"31%\",\n            \"100%\",\n            \"1.00\",\n            \"0.31\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"B-IAVR\",\n            \"27%\",\n            \"68%\",\n            \"0.72\",\n            \"0.375\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"random-p=0.5\",\n            \"26%\",\n            \"50%\",\n            \"0.55\",\n            \"0.473\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"confidence-thresh\",\n            \"25%\",\n            \"55%\",\n            \"0.60\",\n            \"0.417\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"no-verify\",\n            \"22%\",\n            \"0%\",\n            \"0.45\",\n            \"0.489\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"B-IAVR 在 absolute Pareto efficiency 上优于 baselines 但 margin 小。Random baseline 意外 competitive，说明 'when to verify' 的 learned signal 价值有限 at this performance level。Paper 需要 downplay Claim 3 到 'preliminary evidence that learned selective policy outperforms naive baselines' level。可能需要 Plan B（更强 base agent）才能让 selective verification story 有说服力。\\n\\nMedian 档下各 baseline 表现：(1) No-verify 比 always-on 低 9pp（verification 有 value 但不 dramatic），(2) Random-p50 在 50% verify rate 下只丢 5pp（说明 selective 的 marginal value 有限——random 就能保留大部分 benefit），(3) Confidence threshold 与 random 接近（model confidence 不是 good proxy for informativeness at 30% success level）。B-IAVR 优于 random 和 confidence 但优势小（1-2pp at matched cost），因为 action-change signal 本身 noisy。Pareto frontier analysis 中 B-IAVR 不 clearly dominate——接近 random baseline 的 performance。这削弱了 Claim 3 的独立贡献。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"No-verify ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"Episode-level GRPO without self-verification, lower bound\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"success_rate\": 0.22,\n      \"action_is_valid\": 0.58,\n      \"vs_always_on_delta\": -9,\n      \"avg_episode_length\": 18\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"9pp delta 证明 verification 有 non-trivial value，支撑了 selective verification 的 motivation。但 delta 不够大（<10pp），使 cost-saving story 的 potential 有限——即使完美 selective，最多能恢复 9pp 中的大部分。\\n\\nNo-verify 比 always-on 低 9pp（median 档 expectation）。Verification 的主要价值在于 error recovery——检测并修正 invalid/ineffective actions。在 30% success 的 agent 中，roughly 1/3 的 success 来自 verification-triggered correction（30% × 0.3 ≈ 9pp contribution）。但 delta 只有 9pp 而非更大，因为：(1) 72% verification 是 confirmatory（不改变行为），(2) 部分 action change 是 noise 而非 correction，(3) 一些任务不需要 verification 就能完成（simple pick tasks）。这验证了 verification 有 value 但也说明 always-on 的 inefficiency（72% 浪费）。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Entropy-controlled action-change analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"Partial correlation of action-change with success after controlling for policy entropy\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"raw_correlation\": 0.15,\n      \"partial_correlation_entropy_controlled\": 0.11,\n      \"p_value\": 0.038,\n      \"high_entropy_stratum_correlation\": 0.08,\n      \"low_entropy_stratum_correlation\": 0.14,\n      \"medium_entropy_stratum_correlation\": 0.12\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Stratified correlation analysis\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"entropy_stratum\",\n          \"n\",\n          \"action_change_rate\",\n          \"correlation\",\n          \"p_value\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"low (<0.1)\",\n            \"180\",\n            \"18%\",\n            \"0.14\",\n            \"0.06\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"medium (0.1-0.3)\",\n            \"250\",\n            \"28%\",\n            \"0.12\",\n            \"0.05\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"high (>0.3)\",\n            \"120\",\n            \"42%\",\n            \"0.08\",\n            \"0.38\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Signal exists but is weak and barely significant. Defense against 'action change = noise' is partial: can say 'signal persists after entropy control' but effect size is small. Honest paper would acknowledge this as limitation and position action-change as 'best available proxy' rather than 'validated signal'.\\n\\nMedian 档定义 action-change partial correlation 0.10-0.20，取 0.11 after controlling entropy。Raw correlation 从 0.15 降到 0.11（entropy 解释了部分 variance，说明 high-entropy states 确实倾向于产生 action change 而非 informed correction）。P-value 0.038 刚过 significance threshold 但不 compelling（reviewer 可能要求 Bonferroni correction 后不再 significant）。Low-entropy stratum correlation 更高（0.14）说明在 confident states 中 action change 更可能是 informative signal，而 high-entropy 中更可能是 noise。这是 partial defense 但不是 strong evidence。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Causal intervention: random vs verification-triggered changes\",\n    \"description\": \"Inject random action changes vs verification-triggered, compare success\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"verification_triggered_success\": 0.32,\n      \"random_triggered_success\": 0.24,\n      \"no_change_baseline_success\": 0.28,\n      \"delta_triggered_vs_random\": 8,\n      \"delta_triggered_vs_nochange\": 4\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Causal intervention results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"condition\",\n          \"success_rate\",\n          \"n_episodes\",\n          \"vs_baseline\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"verification-triggered change\",\n            \"32%\",\n            \"200\",\n            \"+4pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"no change (baseline)\",\n            \"28%\",\n            \"200\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"random change (same rate)\",\n            \"24%\",\n            \"200\",\n            \"-4pp\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Provides causal evidence that verification adds value (not just noise). But effect size moderate (+4pp vs baseline, +8pp vs random). Combined with entropy analysis, forms a 'converging evidence' argument for action-change being a real signal, even if weak individually.\\n\\nMedian 档下 verification-triggered changes 比 random changes 好 8pp。原因：verification 过程给 model 额外 context（重新审视 state），使得 change 更 informed。但 delta 只有 8pp 而非 15+pp（strong 档），因为：(1) 30% success agent 的 verification quality 中等（不是所有 verification-triggered change 都是 correct），(2) random change 有时碰巧也有用（ALFWorld action space 有限，random valid action 有 non-trivial hit rate），(3) 'no change baseline' 成功率 28% 意味着很多 episodes 不需要 correction 就能 succeed/fail。Interesting finding: triggered > no-change > random? No — triggered > no-change, random < no-change. Random changes 实际上 hurt（从 28% → 24%），verification-triggered 才是 helpful。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Reward signal ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"B-IAVR with action-change vs random-trigger vs confidence-based reward\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"action_change_success\": 0.27,\n      \"action_change_verify_rate\": 0.68,\n      \"random_trigger_success\": 0.25,\n      \"random_trigger_verify_rate\": 0.62,\n      \"confidence_reward_success\": 0.24,\n      \"confidence_verify_rate\": 0.7\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Reward signal comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"reward_type\",\n          \"success\",\n          \"verify_rate\",\n          \"cost_reduction\",\n          \"training_stability\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"action-change (ours)\",\n            \"27%\",\n            \"68%\",\n            \"28%\",\n            \"moderate (converges step 40)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"random trigger\",\n            \"25%\",\n            \"62%\",\n            \"35%\",\n            \"unstable (high variance)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"confidence-based\",\n            \"24%\",\n            \"70%\",\n            \"26%\",\n            \"slow convergence\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Action-change is best but advantage is modest (2-3pp). Paper can claim 'action-change outperforms baselines' but the weak margin means a reviewer could argue the differences are within noise. Need to frame carefully with error bars and multiple seeds.\\n\\nMedian 档下 action-change reward 优于 alternatives 但 margin 小。Action-change (27%, verify 68%) vs random-trigger (25%, verify 62%) delta = 2pp success, +6pp verify rate。原因：(1) random trigger reward 无 informative signal，模型学到的 verify 策略接近 uniform random，(2) confidence-based reward 在 1.7B model 上不好估计（model 的 logit calibration 差，confidence 不 correlate well with actual uncertainty），(3) action-change 虽然 noisy 但至少有 partial signal（r=0.11）。Margin 小因为 base signal 本身弱——在 strong 档下差异会更明显。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"ARES reproduction + comparison\",\n    \"description\": \"Reproduce ARES SFT router on ALFWorld, head-to-head with B-IAVR\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"ares_success\": 0.26,\n      \"ares_verify_rate\": 0.58,\n      \"ares_cost_reduction\": 0.38,\n      \"biavr_success\": 0.27,\n      \"biavr_verify_rate\": 0.68,\n      \"biavr_cost_reduction\": 0.28,\n      \"delta_success\": 1,\n      \"delta_cost\": -10\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"ARES vs B-IAVR head-to-head\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"success\",\n          \"verify_rate\",\n          \"cost_reduction\",\n          \"training_data_needed\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"ARES (SFT router)\",\n            \"26%\",\n            \"58%\",\n            \"38%\",\n            \"oracle labels required\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"B-IAVR (RL)\",\n            \"27%\",\n            \"68%\",\n            \"28%\",\n            \"no labels (self-supervised)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"always-on\",\n            \"31%\",\n            \"100%\",\n            \"0%\",\n            \"—\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"ARES comparison doesn't favor our method on cost reduction. Differentiation must come from methodology (no oracle labels needed, RL-based adaptation) rather than performance numbers. Paper should frame as 'comparable performance without supervision' rather than 'superior performance'.\\n\\nARES 使用 SFT router（从 oracle labels 学 when to verify），在 cost reduction 上优于 B-IAVR（38% vs 28%）但 success 相近（26% vs 27%）。原因：(1) SFT 有 direct supervision signal（teacher-labeled 'should verify here'），训练更 clean，(2) 但 SFT labels 是 frozen（从一个 checkpoint 生成），不 adapt to policy improvement，所以 success 不如 RL-trained 的 B-IAVR，(3) ARES 的 continuous effort allocation 在 ALFWorld binary 场景中退化为 threshold，效果有限。Head-to-head 中 B-IAVR 不 clearly dominate ARES — 不同 trade-off point。这削弱了 'B-IAVR dominates' 的 claim。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"ScienceWorld transfer\",\n    \"description\": \"Episode-level vs step-independent on ScienceWorld environment\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"episode_level_success\": 0.18,\n      \"step_independent_success\": 0.04,\n      \"improvement_ratio\": 4.5,\n      \"episode_level_std\": 0.05,\n      \"convergence_slower\": true,\n      \"steps_to_plateau\": 25\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"ScienceWorld transfer results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"success_rate\",\n          \"improvement_vs_step_ind\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"step-independent (h=2)\",\n            \"4%\",\n            \"baseline\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"step-independent (h=10)\",\n            \"9%\",\n            \"2.3x\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"episode-level GRPO\",\n            \"18%\",\n            \"4.5x\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Supports generalization: dual mechanism failure is not ALFWorld-specific. But low absolute numbers (18%) limit the impact claim. Paper can use this as 'consistent across environments' evidence for Claim 1 diagnostic.\\n\\nMedian 档下 transfer 到 ScienceWorld 仍显示 episode-level 优势（4.5x）但 absolute performance 较低（18% vs ALFWorld 的 30%）。原因：(1) ScienceWorld 比 ALFWorld 更复杂（更长 episode、更大 action space、partial observability），(2) 1.7B 模型在 science reasoning 上能力有限，(3) step-independent 在更长 horizon（ScienceWorld 40-50 步）下崩溃更严重（4% vs ALFWorld 的 3%），(4) 收敛更慢因为 reward 更 sparse。Results 支持 generalization claim 但 18% absolute performance 不算 impressive。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"7B model scaling verification\",\n    \"description\": \"Episode-level vs step-independent on Qwen3-7B\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"episode_7b_success\": 0.42,\n      \"step_ind_7b_success\": 0.08,\n      \"improvement_ratio\": 5.25,\n      \"episode_7b_vs_1.7b_delta\": 10,\n      \"step_ind_7b_vs_1.7b_delta\": 5\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Model size scaling\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"model\",\n          \"episode-level\",\n          \"step-ind (h=2)\",\n          \"ratio\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Qwen3-1.7B\",\n            \"32%\",\n            \"3%\",\n            \"10.7x\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen3-7B\",\n            \"42%\",\n            \"8%\",\n            \"5.3x\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Supports Claim 1: step-independent failure is structural, not a model capacity issue. 7B cannot compensate for broken credit assignment. Episode-level benefits from scale as expected. Ratio decreases (10.7x→5.3x) but absolute gap increases (29pp→34pp).\\n\\nMedian 档下 7B 模型 episode-level 达到 42%（vs 1.7B 的 32%），step-independent 仍 collapse 到 8%（vs 1.7B 的 3%，7B 有更好 base capabilities 所以 collapse 后仍保留一些）。Episode-level 的 10pp 提升来自 larger model 的 better base reasoning/planning。Step-independent 的 slight improvement（8% vs 3%）因为 7B 在短 window 内也能做更好的 local decisions，但 sign misattribution 仍然阻止真正的 improvement。Key finding: scaling 不能 fix step-independent 的 structural problem（8% 仍远低于 episode-level 的 42%）。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Per-task-type breakdown\",\n    \"description\": \"ALFWorld success breakdown by task type for episode-level\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"put_success\": 0.4,\n      \"clean_success\": 0.32,\n      \"heat_success\": 0.28,\n      \"cool_success\": 0.3,\n      \"examine_success\": 0.18,\n      \"pick_two_success\": 0.15,\n      \"correlation_with_length\": -0.72,\n      \"short_task_advantage\": 12\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Per-task breakdown (episode-level, step 15)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"task_type\",\n          \"success\",\n          \"avg_steps\",\n          \"action_is_valid\",\n          \"n_val\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"put\",\n            \"40%\",\n            \"12.3\",\n            \"62%\",\n            \"10\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"clean\",\n            \"32%\",\n            \"18.7\",\n            \"55%\",\n            \"6\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"cool\",\n            \"30%\",\n            \"16.2\",\n            \"58%\",\n            \"4\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"heat\",\n            \"28%\",\n            \"17.8\",\n            \"53%\",\n            \"4\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"examine\",\n            \"18%\",\n            \"24.5\",\n            \"48%\",\n            \"3\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"pick_two\",\n            \"15%\",\n            \"28.1\",\n            \"45%\",\n            \"5\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Confirms intuition: episode-level advantage is largest for simpler tasks where credit can be assigned more cleanly. Complex tasks remain challenging even with episode-level training — potential direction for future work (hierarchical RL or subgoal decomposition). Useful for paper's 'limitation' section.\\n\\nMedian 档下 per-task 差异明显：simple tasks（put: 40%）远好于 complex tasks（examine: 18%, pick_two: 15%）。原因：(1) 短 episode tasks（put 通常 10-15 步）在 episode-level 下 credit assignment 更 focused（fewer actions dilute the signal），(2) Complex tasks 需要 multi-step planning（先找 object、再找 tool、再执行），30% overall success 的 agent 在需要 3+ correct decisions 的 task 上 success 急剧下降，(3) pick_two 需要 remember 两个 target objects——working memory challenge for 1.7B。Length-success correlation -0.72 confirms episode complexity is key difficulty factor。\"\n  }\n]","numLines":876,"startLine":1,"totalLines":876}}}
